From 6fb2c2860cc352d510fc9809e55c484e8f836079 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antoine Pichot <antoine.pichot@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:44:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] media: i2c: ov7251: Use in-range PLL1 dividers for the
 319.2 MHz link

The 19.2 MHz PLL1 table for the 319.2 MHz link frequency sets the PLL1
pre-divider (register 0x30B4, bits [3:0], a coded field where 0x04 means
divide by 4) to 0x01, which the datasheet decodes as divide by 1, and
the PLL1 divider (register 0x30B1, bits [4:0], a literal divisor from 1
to 16) to 0x04. With a 19.2 MHz external clock and the multiplier of
0x85 (133), the PLL1 multiplier output, the VCO of figure 2-12, runs at
19.2 x 133 = 2553.6 MHz before the divider brings it down to 638.4 MHz.
Table 2-11 of the OV7750/OV7251 datasheet (rev 2.12) limits the PLL1
multiplier output to 300 to 800 MHz, so the current values run the
oscillator at 3.2 times the datasheet maximum.

Divide before multiplying instead: pre-divider 0x04 (divide by 4, a
4.8 MHz reference) and divider 0x01. The multiplier output is then
4.8 x 133 = 638.4 MHz, inside the allowed range, and the MIPI clock
after the unchanged MIPI divider (0x30B5 = 0x05, divide by 1) is the
same 638.4 Mbps as before, so the 319.2 MHz link frequency and the
63.84 MHz pixel rate do not change.

This is the arrangement the Intel ov7251 Windows driver
(30.18305.6.5127) programs for its Windows Hello 30 fps mode on the
Surface Book 2: 0x30B4 = 0x04, 0x30B3 = 0x85, 0x30B1 = 0x01,
0x30B0 = 0x0a, 0x30B5 = 0x05. The 240 MHz tables, the 24 MHz tables
and the PLL2 tables of the series are untouched.

Test patch for the Surface Pro 7+ link report on patch 1 of the series;
not for merging as is.

Signed-off-by: Antoine Pichot <antoine.pichot@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
index 1413f1856e3b..1f30a01c85b3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov7251.c
@@ -174,9 +174,9 @@ static const struct ov7251_pll1_cfg ov7251_pll1_cfg_19_2_mhz_240_mhz = {
 };
 
 static const struct ov7251_pll1_cfg ov7251_pll1_cfg_19_2_mhz_319_2_mhz = {
-	.pre_div = 0x01,
+	.pre_div = 0x04,
 	.mult = 0x85,
-	.div = 0x04,
+	.div = 0x01,
 	.pix_div = 0x0a,
 	.mipi_div = 0x05,
 };
